The program first checks if the array is empty. If it is, it returns -1, since there is no element to search for. If the array is not empty, it calculates the midpoint of the array and checks if the target value is equal to the element at the midpoint. If it is, it returns the index of the midpoint.

If the target value is less than the element at the midpoint, the program recursively calls the binary_search function on the first half of the array. If the target value is greater than the element at the midpoint, the program recursively calls the binary_search function on the second half of the array.

The program continues recursively dividing the array in half until it finds the target value or determines that it is not present. Once it finds the target value, it returns the index of the element. If it determines that the target value is not present, it returns -1.

