```python
import getCurrentDate from '../api/get-current-date';

export async function handler(req, res) {
  try {
    const { date } = await getCurrentDate();
    res.status(200).json({ date });
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(500).json({ error: error.message });
  }
}

export default handler;
```
This code defines a route that will be handled by the `getCurrentDate` function. When a request is made to the `/api/current-date` endpoint, the `handler` function will be called, which will then call the `getCurrentDate` function to get the current date and time. The response will be a JSON object with a `date` property containing the current date and time in ISO format.

