Inheritance allows for code reuse and can make your code more organized and readable. It also allows for a more natural and intuitive class hierarchy.

You can also use inheritance to create a hierarchy of classes, where a subclass can inherit properties and methods from multiple superclasses. This is known as multiple inheritance.
