Object pooling is a technique where you create a pool of objects that can be reused instead of creating new objects every time you need them. This can help reduce the amount of memory used by your program and can also improve performance by reducing the overhead of object creation and destruction.

To implement object pooling in Python, you can use a list or a dictionary to store a pool of objects. When you need a new object, you can check the pool to see if there are any available objects that can be reused. If there are no available objects, you can create a new object as usual.

